        "id": 1041767
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-12T21:19:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that brings up the fundamental problem with this module.\n\n`Storage` isn\u0027t at all storage, but a thin wrapper around the bt configuration settings and run time data accumulated (other devices)\n\nI don\u0027t like `Storage` nor do I like `Config`",
      "parentUuid": "f70b5569_5206806e",
      "revId": "60dc72c5ddc0c6081d75972a2c81844534959ef2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cb9f81b1_7acf7045",
        "filename": "system/gd/storage/storage_module.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 271,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-12T22:44:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m having a hard time coming up with a good name, since it contains information about the local adapter and about paired devices, but not interoperability information, GATT cache, etc.",
      "parentUuid": "c5a16d86_b03b04ec",
      "revId": "60dc72c5ddc0c6081d75972a2c81844534959ef2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6bbf5467_30b29ee8",
        "filename": "system/gd/storage/storage_module.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 140,
      "author": {
        "id": 1041767
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-12T20:37:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since all these APIs operate on the *data* not the *storage module*, does it make sense to also provide a similar API ?\n\ne.g.\nclass StorageModule\n  struct Data {\n    bool HasSection(..);\n    ...\n  };\n  \nThe argument against this is there is already precedent for this in the public Storage API.",
      "revId": "60dc72c5ddc0c6081d75972a2c81844534959ef2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "616caed5_8409edb4",
        "filename": "system/gd/storage/storage_module.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 140,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-12T20:43:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s the way it was with GetConfigCache().  The problem I had was that if I give away a pointer to the data, my locks are pretty useless.\n\n\"Storage\" -\u003e ConfigFile :)",
      "parentUuid": "6bbf5467_30b29ee8",
      "revId": "60dc72c5ddc0c6081d75972a2c81844534959ef2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0673e231_0a90769b",
        "filename": "system/gd/storage/storage_module.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 140,
      "author": {
        "id": 1041767
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-12T21:19:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Exactly !  I\u0027ve seen this pattern before in the code where we lock, say things are good, then give up the lock/resource, and think all is well.\n\nThe stack lifecycle is a good example of this.\n\nMy proposal still uses the locks as you intended, just a narrower namespace that maintains the lockability.",
      "parentUuid": "616caed5_8409edb4",
      "revId": "60dc72c5ddc0c6081d75972a2c81844534959ef2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
